---
/* nørma on the AOH site: a short introduction that hands over to joinnorma.com,
   which tells the full story. Copy follows joinnorma.com where the old page
   differed (for example, groups of five or more, not ten). */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="nørma · The wellbeing platform from The Artistry of Humanity" description="nørma is the new platform from The Artistry of Humanity: an app for your people and a dashboard for leaders, built on the Five Pillars of Fulfilment. Leaders see groups of five or more, never individuals." path="/what-we-do/norma">

  <!-- What it is -->
  <section class="bg-dark" style="overflow:hidden">
    <div class="glow" style="left:50%;top:-34%;width:80%;transform:translateX(-50%);background:radial-gradient(closest-side,rgba(217,234,110,.16),rgba(217,234,110,0) 70%)"></div>
    <div class="wrap center" style="position:relative;padding-top:clamp(56px,8vw,110px);padding-bottom:clamp(120px,14vw,190px)">
      <img class="n-icon" src="/assets/norma-app-icon.png" alt="" width="224" height="224" />
      <span class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:30px">New from The Artistry of Humanity</span>
      <h1 style="color:var(--on-dark);max-width:15em;margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">Meet <span class="it">nørma</span>: an app for your people and <span class="mk mk-d">a dashboard for you</span>.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">Our new platform, built on the Five Pillars of Fulfilment. Your people see where their life is at. You see where your culture is at, and what to do about it.</p>
      <div class="btns">
        <a class="btn btn-lime" href="https://joinnorma.com/">Explore nørma ↗</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://joinnorma.com/book-a-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Why AOH built it -->
  <section class="lift" style="background:var(--cream)">
    <div class="wrap sec split">
      <figure style="margin:0" data-rv>
        <div class="photo" style="aspect-ratio:3/2"><img src="/assets/workshop.jpg" alt="Ian Williams facilitating a workshop in a full room" width="1024" height="683" loading="lazy" /></div>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Why we built it</span>
        <h2>The work in the room, <span class="mk">kept going</span>.</h2>
        <p class="lead">In our keynotes and workshops, people get honest about where their life is at, and leaders hear what is really going on. But a session is one day. Then the room empties and the year takes over.</p>
        <p class="body">nørma keeps that work going, every month, for every team. A short check-in for each person, a clear picture for leaders, and a session to run with the team when something needs attention. Next month shows whether it moved.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The two sides -->
  <section class="bg-sand lift-b">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="narrow center">
        <span class="eyebrow">One system, both sides</span>
        <h2>The problem has two sides. So does nørma.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split n-row" style="margin-top:clamp(48px,6vw,80px)">
        <figure class="n-phone-wrap" data-rv>
          <div class="n-phone"><img src="/assets/app-where-you-stand.webp" alt="The nørma app after a monthly check-in, showing a score across the Five Pillars" width="780" height="1688" loading="lazy" /></div>
        </figure>
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Your people</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px)">Their life comes to work with them.</h3>
          <p class="body">Work is one pillar of five. Once a month, a short check-in shows each person where they are across all five and where the gaps are, and nørma helps them work on them. It’s theirs. Nobody at work can read it.</p>
          <a class="link" href="https://joinnorma.com/your-people/">See the app ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="split n-row n-rev" style="margin-top:clamp(56px,7vw,96px)">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Leaders</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,38px)">The culture they walk into is yours to shape.</h3>
          <p class="body">You see both sides as group figures: how fulfilled your people are, and whether they feel heard, valued and safe to speak. They meet in one number for each group, the nørma Score, so you know where to look first and what to do.</p>
          <a class="link" href="https://joinnorma.com/for-leaders/">See the dashboard ↗</a>
        </div>
        <figure style="margin:0" data-rv>
          <div class="photo" style="border-radius:22px 16px 24px 14px / 16px 24px 14px 22px;background:#F6F5EE"><img src="/assets/dash-hero.webp" alt="The nørma leader dashboard: nørma Score, Fulfilment, Culture and every department" width="1120" height="816" loading="lazy" /></div>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Privacy -->
  <section class="bg-dark lift">
    <div class="wrap sec split">
      <div style="flex:0 1 300px">
        <div class="stat" style="font-size:clamp(88px,11vw,140px)">5+</div>
        <p class="small" style="color:var(--on-dark-muted);margin-top:14px;max-width:16em">people in the smallest group a leader can see. Smaller groups never appear.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
        <h2>Leaders see patterns, <span class="mk mk-d">never people</span>.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Nobody where someone works can read their check-in answers, reflections or recordings. Answers become a group figure before anything reaches a dashboard, and groups below five never appear. A design decision, not a setting.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Hand over to joinnorma.com -->
  <section class="lift-b" style="background:var(--cream)">
    <div class="wrap sec">
      <div class="card-dark center" style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(48px,6vw,80px) clamp(24px,5vw,64px)">
        <img class="n-icon" src="/assets/norma-app-icon.png" alt="" width="224" height="224" style="width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:18px" />
        <h2 style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto;max-width:14em">The full story is at joinnorma.com.</h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">See how the app and the dashboard work, book a demo, or work out what nørma could return for your organisation.</p>
        <div class="btns">
          <a class="btn btn-lime" href="https://joinnorma.com/">Explore nørma ↗</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://joinnorma.com/book-a-demo/">Book a demo ↗</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://joinnorma.com/roi/">Work out your ROI ↗</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="body center" style="margin-top:32px">Rather start in the room? <a class="link" style="margin:0" href="/what-we-do/keynotes-workshops">Book Ian to speak ›</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* aoh.css: .sec resets the side padding that .wrap gives; keep the gutters. */
  .wrap.sec { padding-left: var(--gut); padding-right: var(--gut); }
  /* Base marks the current page in the nav with ink text and an underline,
     which hides the label on the dark nørma pill. Restore the pill here. */
  :global(.nav a.norma[aria-current]) { padding: 0 12px 0 6px; border-bottom: 0; color: var(--on-dark); }
  .n-icon { display: block; width: 96px; height: 96px; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 26px; box-shadow: 0 24px 50px -18px rgba(0, 0, 0, .6); }
  .n-row { align-items: center; }
  .n-phone-wrap { margin: 0; flex: 0 1 380px; display: flex; justify-content: center; }
  .n-phone { width: min(300px, 78vw); padding: 7px; border-radius: 40px; background: #0B140E; box-shadow: 0 40px 80px -30px rgba(20, 35, 26, .55); }
  .n-phone img { width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 390 / 760; object-fit: cover; object-position: top; border-radius: 33px; }
  /* On phones the dashboard row shows the picture first, like the row above. */
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .n-rev > figure { order: -1; } }
</style>
